$('open-presets').onclick=$('choose-preset').onclick=()=>$('library').showModal();$('open-method').onclick=()=>$('methods').showModal();document.querySelectorAll('dialog .close').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>b.closest('dialog').close());for(const d of document.querySelectorAll('dialog'))d.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target===d){const r=d.getBoundingClientRect();if(e.clientX<r.left||e.clientX>r.right||e.clientY<r.top||e.clientY>r.bottom)d.close();}});
$('method-content').innerHTML=`<div class="method-stats"><div><strong>${number(meta.streets)}</strong><span>ward street segments</span></div><div><strong>${number(meta.poiCount)}</strong><span>POIs, including the buffer</span></div><div><strong>${number(meta.nodes)}</strong><span>routing junctions</span></div></div><h3>Real geography, declared assumptions</h3><p>Street and POI locations come from OpenStreetMap. Data snapshot: <strong>${esc(meta.osmTimestamp)}</strong>. Ward outline: OSM relation ${meta.boundaryRelation}. Neighbouring destinations reduce boundary effects; the routing graph still has a finite outer boundary.</p><h3>How streets are calculated</h3><ul><li>Walking time = shortest retained road distance ÷ walking speed, plus the facility’s straight connector to its nearest retained junction. Connectors over 350 m are excluded. Entrances, signals, slopes and opening hours are not modelled.</li><li>Public primary, secondary, tertiary, residential, unclassified and pedestrian streets are retained. Service alleys and footpaths are omitted. Degree-two shape points are simplified without changing retained path lengths. ${number(meta.discardedDisconnectedNodes)} disconnected source nodes are excluded.</li><li>POI indicators read two endpoints; streets longer than 200 m also read their midpoint. Samples have equal weights before the selected power mean.</li><li>Mean depth, closeness and harmonic centrality use all buffered junctions as targets, excluding self. Street scores combine two endpoint values. Betweenness is the raw, exact, undirected edge measure.</li><li>Precomputed route lengths use metres stored as float32. Parameters recalculate real numerical values locally.</li></ul><h3>Five destination categories</h3><p>${meta.categories.map(c=>`${esc(c.name)}: ${c.count} (${c.insideCount} inside the ward)`).join(' · ')}.</p><p>POIs are mapped entities, not an exhaustive official register. ${meta.deduplicatedPois} same-name, same-type records within 90 m were deduplicated; ${meta.excludedFarPois} facilities with long connectors were excluded.</p><h3>Supply and competition are scenarios</h3><p>Equal weights count every facility once. Type weights assign 4 to hospitals and universities; 3 to supermarkets; 2 to schools, colleges, parks, sports centres, libraries and community centres; 1 to other mapped types. These are assumptions, <strong>not measured capacity</strong>.</p><p>Competition uses <strong>one demand unit at each retained inside-ward junction</strong>, not census population. Benefit kernels use the same distance kernel in both steps. Walking-cost and constant readouts use an exponential demand kernel with β = 0.08 per minute. γ changes the relative preference for less-contested facilities; it is not calibrated behaviour.</p><h3>Read the legend</h3><p>Choose Colors in the header or legend to select one of 12 palettes, reverse its direction, or set your own three colors. The legend always runs from low numerical values on the left to high values on the right. The default is blue for low values and red for high values. Higher walking-time values mean longer journeys. Color settings do not change calculated scores and are remembered in this browser. Colours use the current 5th–95th percentiles; extreme colours are clipped, not the values. Compare displayed raw values between configurations. Grey means an unmet quota or undefined score.</p><h3>What the classic names guarantee</h3><p>A classic label appears when the parameters satisfy that mathematical family. The stated graph, supply, demand and street-aggregation assumptions still apply. The site does not claim to reproduce DepthmapX, NAIN or NACH.</p><h3>Sources & reproducibility</h3><p><a target="_blank" href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OSM contributors · ODbL 1.0</a> · <a target="_blank" href="https://maps.gsi.go.jp/development/">GSI background tiles</a> · <a target="_blank" href="https://www.niu.edu/landform/papers/Luo_Wang2003.pdf">Luo & Wang, 2003</a> · <a target="_blank" href="https://www.niu.edu/landform/papers/JHAP741_e2sfca.pdf">Luo & Qi, 2009</a> · <a target="_blank" href="https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/centrality.html">Centrality definitions</a></p><p>Geometry, POIs, route tables, centralities and 29 GSI tiles are bundled. No account or API key is required. Background tiles are cached through zoom 13 and enlarged at closer zooms; street geometry stays sharp. <a href="guide.html" target="_blank">Complete parameter guide ↗</a></p>`;
